# Myket (مایکت)

> Myket is an Iranian Android app store and digital content platform serving Persian-speaking users. It distributes Android apps and games directly as APK files, and also provides video content and app publishing services for developers.

Most consumer-facing content is in Persian (fa-IR). Myket offers hundreds of thousands of Android apps and games from Iranian and international developers. Distribution happens through the Myket Android client, not through Google Play.

Myket's main web resources are: `myket.ir` is the consumer website and catalog, `developer.myket.ir` is the developer portal for publishing and managing apps, and `myket.ir/kb/` holds developer technical documentation.

On conflicting information: an individual app page is authoritative for that app's own metadata; the developer knowledge base is authoritative for publishing, in-app purchase, SDK, and developer policy; the policy pages are authoritative for terms, privacy, and copyright rules.

App metadata is volatile. Version, size, rating, download count, and whether an app is still published must be read from that app's current page at the time of use, not cached or inferred from elsewhere.

## Main sections

- [Home](https://myket.ir/): Main consumer website.
- [Apps](https://myket.ir/apps): Android application catalog.
- [Games](https://myket.ir/games): Android game catalog.
- [AI](https://myket.ir/ai): AI application catalog, including image and video generation.
- [Video](https://myket.ir/video): Movies, series, and animation with Persian dubbing and subtitles.
- [Movies](https://myket.ir/video/movie): Film catalog, dubbed or subtitled in Persian, with online streaming.
- [Series](https://myket.ir/video/series): Series catalog, dubbed or subtitled in Persian, with online streaming.
- [Myket TV](https://myket.ir/tv): Watching the video catalog on TV, and the Android TV app.

## URL patterns

- [Application example](https://myket.ir/app/com.kiloo.subwaysurf): App pages use `/app/{packageName}`; the Android package name identifies the app. Pages provide app metadata, descriptions, screenshots, and selected user reviews where available. A subset of this information is also available as schema.org `SoftwareApplication` structured data.
- [Developer example](https://myket.ir/developer/creator-8369): Developer pages use `/developer/{developerId}`.
- [Category example](https://myket.ir/games/casual): Categories use `/{apps|games}/{category}`.

